    <item>
      <title>Research</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;My research focuses on mechanics-informed intelligent systems for monitoring, modelling, and decision-making in civil infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;h3&gt;Structural Health Monitoring&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Vibration-based and data-driven methods for damage detection, localization, and condition assessment of civil infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;h3&gt;Digital Twins&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Mechanics-informed digital twins that combine sensing data, computational models, and AI for infrastructure state estimation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;h3&gt;Physics-Informed Machine Learning&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Machine learning models constrained by governing equations, continuum mechanics, and physical principles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;h3&gt;Computer Vision for Infrastructure&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Image and video-based methods for displacement tracking, vibration measurement, crack detection, and inspection.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>About</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/about/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/about/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Prof. Ashish Pal is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Civil Engineering at the Indian Institute of Technology Bombay. His research lies at the intersection of structural engineering, scientific computing, sensing technologies, and artificial intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;His work focuses on developing mechanics-informed intelligent systems for structural health monitoring, digital twins, scientific machine learning, and resilient infrastructure monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Research Vision&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;research-vision&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#research-vision&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The long-term goal of the research is to develop intelligent infrastructure systems capable of autonomous sensing, interpretation, prediction, and decision support through the integration of mechanics, sensing technologies, data, and machine intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
